{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120609","id":3928091988,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7qIe1U","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120609","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120609.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120609.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120609","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120609/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120609/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120609/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/a5a337876c814c2a1307a95fe2dd351747d50ba8","number":120609,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add `BoneSpaceAdjuster3D` & `skin_scale` property to Bone in Skeleton3D","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/4190\r\n- Supersedes/Closes #83903\r\n\r\nWhen scaling is applied to a bone, children inherit the parent’s scale. Some ideas have been proposed in #83903 and https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/79364#issuecomment-4407306875 to remove this inheritance, but that would break consistency with Node3D’s calculation method and create new problems dependent on whether inheritance is enabled or not. We can state with almost certainty that no such change will occur, at least until Godot 5.\r\n\r\nHowever, the issue of scaling being difficult to handle remains, so this PR will address for that case in some extent.\r\n\r\nThis PR will add `SkinScale` as a property of the bone. This will allow us to change only the visual scale of the skin bound to the bone without affecting `bone_pose`. This approach was discussed with @lyuma before.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"521\" height=\"139\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bf5aed54-d10b-4d2f-b6c1-d7e5c8d5a36d\" />\r\n\r\nSince `SkinScale` is calculated only when passing skin information to the rendering server during bone updates, this scaling will not be retained on the `MeshInstance`’s skin resource side. If `skin_scale` is a Vector3(1, 1, 1), a boolean cache is maintained to avoid calculating the scaling.\r\n\r\nIf there is a drawback compared to applying scaling directly to `bone_pose`, it is that this method cannot be used to change the length of the bone. In other words, the position of child objects will not synchronize with the scaling applied by `skin_scale`.\r\n\r\nIf you want to synchronize the child’s position, you can convert the scaling along the parent-to-child axis to a position and set it to the child’s `bone_pose_position` to achieve synchronization with the scaling. Even without that, this approach should be sufficient  usable for applications where you simply want to change the thickness without change bone structures.\r\n\r\n_Edited:_\r\n\r\nI added a BoneSpreader to adjust the positions of child bones. We should not change the skin within the SkeletonModifier. However, this is safe because the roles are clearly separated, like \"the Skeleton modifies change the skin\" and \"the SkeletonModifier modifies change the bone position\".\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1159\" height=\"610\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/33601d2c-8c74-46ca-a94d-2f6fd9759ab8\" />\r\n\r\nAdditionally, since this involves moving the position rather than scaling from the sight of bone transform, it is compatible with IK.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"448\" height=\"323\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bff8f5d6-3b27-4854-be0d-28a4e9b2c6ef\" />\r\n\r\nBTW, you must be careful when using this with RetargetModifier in retargeting mode. In cases where this feature is used, it is probably better to use the OverwriteRest retargeting method, which does not use RetargetModifier. If you absolutely must use RetargetModifier, you need to be careful about synchronizing the SkinScale between GeneralSkeleton and OriginalSkeleton.\r\n\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666705648,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA1NjQ4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:animation","name":"topic:animation","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/miles